- timestamp: "2026-07-02T13:00:00Z"
  actor: claude
  action: session-work
  item: "bitnet-refinement"
  summary: >
    Added native TL2 GGUF support: GGML_TYPE_TL2 (dtype 39) and TL1 (dtype 38)
    detection in GGUF loader, Tl2Tensor struct with dimension metadata + extracted
    scale, runtime dispatch in both forward_bitnet_decode and forward_quantized
    (TL2 → I2S fallback). Added Tl2Config::for_dims() with auto BM selection and
    tl2_forward() top-level dispatch. Patched bitnet.cpp converter to handle
    BitNetForCausalLM architecture, converted model to TL2 format. TL2 GGUF loads
    and dispatches to TL2 kernel but produces wrong output — converter tiling
    parameters (bmm/by) need alignment with kernel expectations. I2S path unchanged
    and verified: coherent output, ~19 tok/s, 326 tests passing.

- timestamp: "2026-07-02T12:30:00Z"
  actor: claude
  action: session-work
  item: "bitnet-refinement"
  summary: >
    BitNet pure translation audit + fix session. Diagnosed and fixed forward_bitnet_decode
    "correctness bug" — root cause was forward_quantized using CpuRMSNorm (f32) for
    attn_sub_norm/ffn_sub_norm while forward_bitnet_decode correctly used CpuRMSNormGgml
    (f64, matching ggml.c). Error compounded across layers (0.66 max_diff over 3 layers).
    Fixed forward_quantized to use det_rmsnorm for sub-norms. Re-enabled forward_bitnet_decode
    dispatch. Cleaned up duplicate buffer declarations and n_threads computation. Added
    comparison test (test_bitnet_decode_matches_quantized). Line-by-line kernel audit via
    3 parallel agents: i2s_quantize_into matches ggml-quants.c, vec_dot_i2_i8_s_avx2 matches
    ggml-bitnet-mad.cpp, tl2.rs matches bitnet-lut-kernels-tl2.h — zero divergences across
    all three. TL2 wiring deferred: model uses I2S format (ggml-model-i2_s.gguf), not TL2.
    In bitnet.cpp these are separate compile-time paths with different GGUF formats. 326 tests
    passing (171 engine + 111 kernels + 44 other).

- timestamp: "2026-06-30T21:15:00Z"
  actor: claude
  action: session-work
  item: "bitnet-refinement"
  summary: >
    BitNet refinement complete. Added 4 I2S unit tests, 4 I2S Kani harnesses,
    1 BitNet e2e forward pass test (314 tests, 61 Kani harnesses).
    Validated against microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf (ggml-model-i2_s.gguf):
    loaded 1.2GB I2S model, extracted tokenizer from GGUF metadata,
    tested 4 prompts — all produce coherent, factually correct output
    ("2+2=4", transformer definition, haiku, prime numbers).
    CPU inference ~1.5 tok/s (scalar). Added AVX2 vec_dot_i2_i8_s_avx2
    (maddubs), AVX2 quantize_row_i8_s_avx2, and rayon-parallel matmul
    in CpuMatMulQ4KOpt::forward_b_transposed_i2s. Result: ~17 tok/s
    (11x speedup). Added test_i2s_avx2_matches_scalar correctness test.
    315 tests passing. Phase 12: 6/7 items done, only TQ2 GPU kernel remaining.

    Validated against bitnet.cpp on same hardware: bitnet.cpp 42.7 tok/s (8 threads),
    tempura 17 tok/s (maddubs+AVX2+rayon). Gap is algorithmic: bitnet.cpp uses
    LUT-based dot product (precompute activation pair sums, use weight nibbles as
    shuffle indices). Translated the LUT approach to Rust:
    - i2s_build_pair_lut: 16-entry i16 LUT per activation pair
    - vec_dot_i2_i8_s_lut_scalar: scalar LUT-based dot product
    - transpose_i2s_weights: column-major weight layout for cache-friendly access
    - forward_i2s_lut: trait method + impls on CpuMatMulQ4K/Q4KOpt
    - Wired into GGUF loader (auto-transpose at load time) and model forward pass
    LUT correctness verified (matches maddubs to <0.01). 317 tests passing.
    Implemented three AVX2 LUT variants:
    (a) i8 LUT (63-scale) + cmpgt sign-extend per position: 10.2 tok/s
    (b) i16 pre-split lo/hi byte LUT (127-scale) + 4 shuffles per position: 6.7 tok/s
    (c) Scalar LUT fallback: ~8 tok/s
    All three are slower than maddubs (17 tok/s) due to per-position LUT load
    overhead — each byte position loads 32-64 bytes of LUT tables from memory.
    bitnet.cpp's speed (42.7 tok/s) comes from BM=160 tiled layout where weights
    are pre-loaded in registers and shared across many output rows. Our transposed
    layout processes 32 columns at once but thrashes L1 with per-position LUT loads.
    Reverted production path to maddubs; LUT infrastructure (trait, tests, transpose)
    retained for future tiled kernel implementation. 317 tests, all passing.

    Translated bitnet.cpp's threading model to Rust:
    - TL2 kernel (tl2.rs): per_tensor_quant, three/two_lut_ctor, three/two_tbl_impl,
      preprocessor, qgemm_lut — direct translation of codegen_tl2.py output
    - SpinBarrier from ggml_barrier (atomic counter spin)
    - PersistentPool: condvar-based, per-worker generation tracking, ~2μs wake
    - forward_bitnet_decode: dedicated BitNet decode path with persistent pool
      per-matmul, pre-allocated i8 quantization buffers (zero Vec allocs per token)
    - i2s_quantize_into: write quantized i8 into pre-allocated buffer
    - i2s_gemv_cols: public column-range GEMV for thread-level slicing
    - Wired into GpuQuantizedInferenceWrapper::forward() server dispatch
    - Microbenchmark: dot product at 42.8 tok/s (matches bitnet.cpp exactly)
    - End-to-end: 19.0 tok/s (bitnet.cpp: 42.7 with 8 threads, 27.3 single-threaded)
    - Gap is condvar wake cost per matmul (~2μs × 210 = 0.4ms) plus DRAM bandwidth
    - 325 tests passing, correct output verified

