  item: "gpu-coop-kernel"
  summary: >
    Intra-block cooperative Q4K GEMV kernel: 32 lanes process one block
    together (4 qs bytes each → 8 elements), coalesced reads, warp shuffle
    reduce per block. Results on RTX 5090 (Qwen3-8B shapes):
    down_proj: 0.508ms → 0.066ms (7.7x, 575 GB/s)
    gate_proj: 0.099ms → 0.051ms (2.0x, 755 GB/s)
    lm_head:   0.633ms → 0.401ms (1.6x, 764 GB/s)
    Projected decode: 64 → 144 tok/s (2.3x improvement)
    vs llama.cpp 209 tok/s: gap closed from 3.3x to 1.5x
  iteration: 9
  max_iterations: 10

- timestamp: "2026-06-22T14:00:00+02:00"
  actor: claude
  action: loop-iteration
  item: "fused-gate-up-gpu"
  summary: >
    Fused gate+up+SiLU GPU kernel: single launch, shared activation read,
    dual Q4K dequant, SiLU×gate in one pass. DualPipeline validation:
    max_rel=0.0 (bit-identical to CPU sequential). BUT 3.4x slower than
    separate coop calls — register pressure kills occupancy. Fusion helps
    on CPU (cache reuse) but hurts on GPU (occupancy > data reuse at 1.8 TB/s).
    llama.cpp doesn't fuse gate+up either. Keeping the kernel as verified
    reference; production path uses separate coop calls.
  iteration: 10
  max_iterations: 10

